    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of what happens on `POST /api/owners`. The request body is an `OwnerFieldsDto` (not the `Owner` entity), the endpoint is served by `OwnerRestControllerV1` (`@RequestMapping(\"/api\")` + generated `/owners`), and essentially all the business logic lives in the controller's private `createOwner(...)` pipeline \u2014 the service/repository is a thin `@Transactional` save.\n\n## Validations (in execution order)\n\n**Before any controller code runs \u2014 Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (via `@Valid`/`@Validated`; any failure \u2192 400 through `ExceptionControllerAdvice`):\n1. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/`'`/`-`-separated parts), `@Size(1..30)`\n2. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n3. `title` \u2014 optional enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR` (bad value \u2192 deserialization error)\n4. `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 optional, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)`\n5. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, non-blank `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..80)`\n6. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (`+`, digits, spaces, `()`/`-`), `@Size(1..30)`\n7. `email` \u2014 optional, `@Pattern`, `@Email`, `@Size(1..255)`\n8. `postcode` \u2014 optional, `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`, `@Size(4..4)`\n9. `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 ISO date binding\n\n> Note: `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")` is on the method, but `petclinic.security.enable=false` in the active config, so `DisableSecurityConfig` (`permitAll`) is active and the check is **inert by default**.\n\n**Inside `createOwner` (after MapStruct maps the DTO \u2192 `Owner`), field normalization + validation, in this exact sub-order** (`normalizeOwnerFields`):\n10. **Address normalization** \u2014 trim/collapse/upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET` etc.; blank after normalization \u2192 `InvalidAddressException` (400)\n11. **Telephone normalize + validate** \u2014 strip to digits, assume `+61` if no `+`, drop leading `0`, require 8\u201315 digits and correct national-number length \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400)\n12. **Email** lower-cased\n13. **Disposable-email domain** rejected (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (400)\n14. **Postcode \u2194 city range** check (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400)\n15. **Future registration date** rejected \u2192 `InvalidRegistrationDateException` (400)\n\n**Then the create-time policy guards:**\n16. **Daily limit** \u2014 \u2265100 owners already registered that day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (429)\n17. **City capacity** \u2014 \u226550 owners in that city \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (409)\n18. **Household duplicate** \u2014 an existing owner shares the derived `householdId` (SHA-256 of lastName+postcode) and the request didn't set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409)\n19. **Identity-key duplicate** \u2014 existing owner with same `telephone|email|householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409)\n\n## Side-effects (in order)\n\n20. Default `registrationDate` to today if null, then **roll forward to the next business day** past weekends/public holidays\n21. Assign **`householdId`** and **`householdSize`**\n22. Set **soft-duplicate flags** `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (same lastName+postcode, different phone; skipped for declared household members) \u2014 no rejection\n23. Assign remaining derived fields: **`namesakeCount`**, **`customerCode`** (`REGION-HASH8`), **`membershipNumber`** (`code-M<YY>`), **`bulkSignupWarning`** (>80 owners that day)\n24. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `@Transactional` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` \u2192 JPA `INSERT` (Spring Data JPA under the `spring-data-jpa` profile). **No JPA lifecycle callbacks, entity listeners, auditing, or application events exist.**\n25. Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`, computing read-only response fields (selfLink, displayName, initials, membershipPoints/level, Luhn check digit, etc.)\n26. **Write an AUDIT log line** (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber)\n27. Set the **`Location` header** `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 Created**\n\nTwo request-level wrappers surround the above: an **`Idempotency-Key` header** cache (a repeated key returns the first result with 200 instead of re-running), and a JMX timing aspect on `@Repository` beans (not part of the create logic).\n\nThe only non-standard note worth flagging: for `POST /api/owners` it's the generated **`OwnerFieldsDto` constraints** that gate the request \u2014 the `Owner` entity's own `@NotEmpty`/E.164 `@Pattern` constraints are not exercised on this path."
  },
